~ start
# talk_to entry point for world-Layla (layla_advanced_overlay launches here).
# the chapter 2 intro cutscene does NOT come through here — chapter2_intro.dialogue
# imports this file and jumps straight to post_wake_intro with actors already staged.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen") == true:
	=> companion_hub

# safety net: talked to before the intro somehow ran. stage the pair the way the
# cutscene hand-off would have, then play the intro.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
=> post_wake_intro

~ post_wake_intro
# step 2.212: Test Run's "Skip Layla Wake Chat" sets this flag; the wake-up talk is then skipped.
if Flags.get_level_flag("dev_skip_layla_wake_chat") == true:
	# step 2.392: the wake-up music (chapter2_intro.dialogue) ends with the skipped talk
	do SoundManager.fade_out_music(3.0)
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen", true)
	=> END
# [post opening cutscene convo with us]
# reached from chapter2_intro.dialogue with Fiona (left) and Layla (right, flipped)
# already on stage over the dimmed live level.
# step 2.372: Layla's expressions from her rig (characters/layla/layla_expressions.json). an open mouth
# on her own lines; while Fiona talks she keeps her pose with her mouth closed. she enters as "base"
# (chapter2_intro.dialogue, or the safety net in ~ start), and the first change lands while she fades in.
# a mock scolding first: hand up, cross brows, held for all three lines
do actor_change("Layla", "scolding")
do actor_change("Fiona", "jacket")
Layla: Fionaaaa! You fell asleep while working again!
Layla: How many times do I need to tell you that you need to rest properly!
Layla: In your own bed! In your own home!
# the same pose with her mouth shut ("stern" is scolding's closed twin)
do actor_change("Layla", "stern")
Player: I know, I know.
Player: I just really got into it. Going home would've broken that flow.
# she lets the scolding go when Fiona asks about the jacket (same pose, a small reaction)
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
do actor_change("Fiona", "jacket_suspicious")
Player: Also, what's this thing over me?
do actor_change("Layla", "admiring")
Layla: It's my jacket. I kept it over you to keep you warm as you slept.
do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
do actor_change("Fiona", "jacket")
Player: Oh.
do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
Layla: Wait, lemme take it off you. I'll put it in my car later.
# step 2.423: she steps up to Fiona, the jacket comes off, and she steps back to her spot
do actor_approach("Layla", "Fiona", 300.0, 0.6)
do wait(0.7)
do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
do wait(0.4)
do actor_step_back("Layla", 0.6)
Player: Thanks, Layla.
Player: What time is it? Has the professor come in yet?
do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
Layla: It's 7:30 right now. The professor doesn't come in until 10, usually.
# the favor: hesitant, then worried, then a comic wail ("whining" is "crying" without the tears)
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: And um... Fiona. Would you still help me with what I asked you yesterday?
Layla: You know, the genomic sequencing thing?
do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
Layla: The professor asked me to show him the results first thing after he arrived.
do actor_change("Layla", "whining")
do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
Layla: If I don't do that, I'm doomed!
# relieved at "Sure" (same pose), held while Fiona goes on
do actor_change("Layla", "eager")
Player: Sure. I can do that. Shouldn't take me more than ten minutes.
do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
Player: You know that you could easily do it yourself though, right?
Player: Objectively, you're smarter than the average undergrad Research Assistant.
Player: If I can do it in 10 minutes, you should know it's possible for you to do in under an hour.
# layla is shy...
do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
Layla: Umm... I'm glad you think that.
# ...then extra shy: the blush comes in here, with a small shrink
do actor_change("Layla", "bashful_talk")
do actor_effect("Layla", "shy")
Layla: I would still like to have you do it for me once, if you don't mind...
Layla: I learn faster when you teach me.
do actor_change("Layla", "bashful")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
Player: No worries. Let's get to the lab ASAP. I need to go home and shower after this.
do actor_change("Layla", "beaming")
do actor_effect("Layla", "bounce")
Layla: Yaaaaay! Thanks Fiona! I owe you one.
do actor_change("Layla", "eager")
Player: Let's go.
# step 2.392: the wake-up music (started in chapter2_intro.dialogue) fades out as the talk ends, and the
# library's ambience comes back up under it. does nothing when no music is playing.
do SoundManager.fade_out_music(3.0)
do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen", true)
=> END

~ companion_hub
# in-world talk_to hub over the dimmed live level. both sprites are staged, mirroring
# the real-world arrangement: layla_character.gd sets layla_player_on_left when the
# interaction fires. facing convention matches the intro: left = unflipped, right = flipped.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_player_on_left") == true:
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Layla", true)
else:
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Fiona", true)
# step 2.405: her theme for as long as you talk (it fades when you leave)
do SoundManager.play_music_track("layla_hub_theme", 1.5)
# step 2.373: Layla's expressions from her rig. she enters as "base"; the first change lands while she fades in.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 3:
	do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
	Layla is following you with glistening eyes.
	Her scent reminds you of lavender drenched in dew.
elif Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "content")
	Layla follows along, humming to herself.
	Her scent reminds you of lavender drenched in dew.
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
	Layla follows a step behind, quieter than usual.
~ hub_return
# step 2.373: her resting face while you pick a topic, by closeness tier (close / neutral / distant).
# every topic comes back here, so this also resets her after each one.
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 3:
	do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
elif Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
	do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
else
	do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
What do you want to say to her?

- Ask about our objective [state={{Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("faculty_floor_unlocked")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("greene_office_keycard_talk_seen")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_keycard_refused")}}-{{Inventory.has_item("jayce_camera")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("greene_office_unlocked")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("layla_waiting_outside_office")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged")}}]
	# step 2.290: the later stages, latest first.
	if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_waiting_outside_office") == true:
		do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
		Player: Layla, wait outside, okay? I'll see if there's anything I can find in the office and come out.
		Player: I don't wanna jeopardize you for something I'm having fun doing.
		# step 2.377: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: ...Fine. I'll wait outside.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
			Layla: You might be having fun doing it, but...
			Layla: I'm benefitting too!
			do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
			Layla: But regardless, I get it.
			do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
			Layla: I'll wait outside, Fiona.
			do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
			if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 3:
				Player: Good girl.
				# flustered, with the blush, set before the push-in and held through it
				do actor_change("Layla", "flustered")
				do actor_focus("Layla", 1.5, 0.4)
				Layla: ...
				do actor_unfocus_all(0.3)
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("greene_office_unlocked") == true:
		Player: Jayce must've opened the office door by now...
		Player: We should hurry. It's getting closer to the professor's arrival time.
		# step 2.374: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
			Layla: Then let's hurry.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "surprised")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
			Layla: Oh no! Let's hurry!
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_keycard_refused") == true and Inventory.has_item("jayce_camera") == true:
		Player: I bet this camera in our hands will scare the living shit outta Jayce.
		# step 2.374: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
			Layla: Good. Let's use it.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Hell yeah! Let's tell him what we've got our hands on!
			do actor_change("Layla", "fierce")
			Layla: And then, GET HIM FIRED!!
			Player: (She seems excited about that...)
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_keycard_refused") == true:
		do actor_change("Fiona", "suspicious")
		Player: We need to find some dirt on that... dirtbag.
		Player: Only then will he cooperate.
		# step 2.374: Layla's expressions (rig)
		do actor_change("Layla", "talking")
		Layla: Bet it won't be that difficult. Given his... nature.
		do actor_change("Layla", "neutral")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
		Player: Yes. But... where should we look?
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("greene_office_keycard_talk_seen") == true:
		Player: So his office is locked. As expected.
		Player: We need to talk to the janitor. He mentioned having a keycard, right?
		# step 2.374: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: He did. Let's go.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
			Layla: He did! Let's go talk to him.
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("faculty_floor_unlocked") == true:
		do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
		Player: So, as I mentioned earlier...
		Player: With the nuclein discovery date failing...
		Player: Our only shot is to look for other clues by breaking into his office...
		# step 2.376: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: ...I don't like it.
			Layla: But fine. I'll come.
			do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "troubled")
			Layla: Umm... yeah.
			do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
			Layla: Even though I'm pretty hesitant about that...
			do actor_change("Layla", "admiring")
			Layla: I'll go with you. This is that important.
			do actor_change("Layla", "warm")
			if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 3:
				# step 2.292: close only (moved here from julian's lead).
				do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
				do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
				Layla: Fiona... what if we can't make it?
				Layla: The professor would never write me a letter of recommendation after that... would he?
				do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
				do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
				Her shoulders slump.
				do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
				Player: Don't worry. We've got this.
				Player: We'll figure it out and get in, one way or another.
				# the brave face
				do actor_change("Layla", "eager")
				Then, as if solely for you, she straightens her back and puts on a brave face.
				do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
				do actor_effect("Layla", "nod")
				Layla: Of course! I trust you.
				do actor_change("Layla", "eager")
		Player: Yep. Let's move on.
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("layla_phone_charged") == true:
		# step 2.291: the date came from layla's phone and hasn't been tried yet.
		Player: We've got the date, through your phone. Let's go enter it now.
		# step 2.376: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Fine. Let's go.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yes! Let's go. February 26, 1869 it is!
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked") == true:
		# step 2.226 / 2.291: julian's lead. the book route stays on these lines (less obvious).
		do actor_change("Fiona", "explain")
		Player: What we need to do now is find the precise date Julian mentioned.
		Player: That's our best lead.
		# step 2.376: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Right. That date.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yes! That DNA-related date!
		do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
		Layla: I wonder how we're gonna figure it out, though...
		do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
		Player: Hmmm.
		Player: I'll find a way, I guess.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Hope so.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
			Layla: Of course!
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given") == true:
		# step 2.222: Jayce couldn't open it, but the password is (probably) a date
		do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
		Player: So, it seems like the janitor can't help us much either...
		Player: But... we do know the password's going to be a date.
		Player: Well, most likely.
		# step 2.374: Layla's expressions (rig)
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Right. A date.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yes! Now we only need to know WHAT date it could be.
		do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
		Layla: We should ask someone!
		do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
		do actor_change("Fiona", "base")
		Player: Probably.
		do actor_change("Fiona", "thinking")
		Player: (But... who?)
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted") == true:
		# step 2.221: the code didn't work, so the plan is now the janitor
		Player: So, we're locked out of the lab, unfortunately.
		Player: I think we should talk to the janitor there.
		Player: What do you think?
		# step 2.373: uneasy about him (hand on chest), a little reassured while Fiona takes the lead
		do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
		Layla: Yeah... let's do that.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: Although, I don't like the way he's been looking at us since we entered the room.
		do actor_change("Layla", "touched")
		Player: Yeah, I get it.
		Player: I'll take the lead. And we'll be cautious.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "hesitant")
			Layla: Got it.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "happy_talk")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "nod")
			Layla: Got it!
	else
		Player: So, just to be clear, Layla. All I need to do is go to the lab with you and help with the sequencing, correct?
		Player: Then I can go home and shower, right?
		# step 2.373: distant, quiet and hands down; otherwise a cheerful promise, then a happy hop
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Yes. That's all. I won't bother you after that.
			do actor_change("Layla", "downcast")
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "explaining_talk")
			Layla: Yes! That's all I want from you. I promise I won't bug you after that.
			do actor_change("Layla", "explaining")
		Player: It's alright. You ain't buggin' me.
		Player: Cool. Let's do this, then.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			do actor_change("Layla", "sad")
			Layla: Thanks.
		else
			do actor_change("Layla", "excited")
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yay! Thanks, Fiona.
	=> hub_return

